  "code_and_contract_findings": [
    "Current-CIR-only immutable generator API; no GT/reference/prior/history/route/seed argument and no external I/O or random state in candidate computations.",
    "Original amplitude30% detector preserved; both modes use the same global magnitude maximum across both RX.",
    "Local prominence and leading-edge segment are distinct; candidate support is only edge+/-1 inside the rising segment with stated floor.",
    "One polarization null allowed. Invalid original frames preserve raw metadata but yield empty pools and no normal/wrong label.",
    "Explicit ignored-boundary peak records added before freeze; whole-array flat RX is not a peak.",
    "Raw fallback included in candidate count; overflow above64 logs all candidates and makes the pool unusable.",
    "Same-mode lobe groups are strict positive-overlap connected components; all support/port/lobe provenance retained.",
    "Evaluator computes Native-LoS reference only after candidate pools exist; fixed exact packet/condition joins and all6320 waveform denominator retained.",
    "Primary recall uses valid>=2tap dynamicFull errors with actual supported reference and no overflow; G4 and Native-LoS are separate controls.",
    "Paired usable gains/losses are retained, including possible union overflow despite strongest tap-set inclusion.",
    "Threshold .95 and per-nonempty-route guard fixed; zero denominator NOT_TESTED; descriptive status cannot imply H2/E2 success.",
    "Strict stage guard binds reviewed code bytes to code-lock and git implementation commit, required document hashes, qualified H0 evidence, owner scoped approval, exact35 actual inputs, and single-thread environment before waveform math or output creation.",
    "Failures preserve partial outputs; existing output directory is refused.",
    "Separate result checker reconstructs Hann/per-port FFT, scalar peaks/edges/groups/candidates, all packet classifications and aggregates without production candidate imports. It shares only identity/stage guard and NumPy FFT runtime."
  ],
